  "name": "Storm Hike",
  "type": "feat",
  "effects": [],
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "gm": "",
      "value": "<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><strong>Requirements</strong> You are in @UUID[Compendium.immortal-ardor.archetypes.vNck1Oor9udzoSRj]{Storm Surge Stance}</p><hr><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin\">Your aerial control grants you greater movements. When you take this feat, you gain the Cat Fall skill feat. If you already have the Cat Fall skill feat, you gain the Rolling Landing skill feat instead.</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin\">While in your stance, if you have the Aspect of Skies, at any point after a Leap before you touch the ground, you can Leap again with an action as your motes propel you further with stormy winds. If you have the Aspect of Tides, your motes instead form a bed of water to dampen your fall as if you intentionally dove in to a 30 foot deep pool of water.</span></p>"
    },
